d in this spot. I will go with "Check".\n\n\n', 'output': "Evaluation: You hold a pair of 4s (4h, 4s) with an Ace and Queen on the board. The opponent has shown passivity by checking pre-flop and on the flop. The pot is small (200 chips). Your hand has showdown value but is vulnerable to any Ace or Queen. Betting here unlikely gets value from worse hands (except perhaps a pair of 3s or a draw) and isolates you against better hands. Checking allows you to control the pot size and attempt to reach a showdown cheaply to realize your hand's equity.\n\nReason: With a low pair on a board with two high overcards (Ace, Queen), the best strategy is to check. The opponent's passivity suggests they might not have a strong hand, but betting offers little reward compared to the risk of being raised or called by a better hand. Checking preserves your stack and gives you a free look at the river.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
