uts if I pair the King. The pot is currently small following a passive pre-flop round where both players checked/called. Since I am leading the overall game by a significant margin (2380 chips) on hand 19 of 20, my strategic priority is to minimize variance and avoid difficult spots that could cost a large portion of my stack.\n\nReason: Checking is the optimal move to control the pot size. Being out of position with a drawing hand, betting opens me up to a raise which would force me to put more chips in without a made hand or fold my equity. Checking allows me to potentially see the Turn card for free to hit my flush, or easily call a standard bet from the opponent given my hand's strength. This plays defensively to protect my cumulative lead while retaining the chance to win the pot if my hand improves.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
