g hits. The game history shows passive play with checks all around on previous streets, keeping the pot very small. Since I am currently leading the overall match by a significant margin (cumulative +2380) and this is hand 19/20, my primary strategic goal is to minimize variance and protect my lead. Building a large pot with only a draw creates unnecessary risk. Checking allows me to see the river card for free. If I hit the flush, I can value bet on the river. If I miss, I can easily fold to a bet without having committed significant chips.\n\nReason: I have a strong flush draw but no made hand yet. Checking allows me to realize my equity for free, keeping the pot small and minimizing the risk of losing a large portion of my stack, which protects my overall cumulative lead late in the game.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
